From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PowerPhone Build <powerphone@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 00:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] audio: do not request undefined PowerPhone device gain

An explicitly present, default-constructed AudioGainConfig is still a gain
request.  The PowerPhone device ports intentionally expose no gain controls,
so the generic AIDL module rejects every startup probe before AudioPolicyManager
can mark the attached BUS devices available.  Leave the optional gain absent.
---
 audio/aidl/default/powerphone/Powerphone.cpp | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/audio/aidl/default/powerphone/Powerphone.cpp b/audio/aidl/default/powerphone/Powerphone.cpp
index 90cb0aa4a..1008da121 100644
--- a/audio/aidl/default/powerphone/Powerphone.cpp
+++ b/audio/aidl/default/powerphone/Powerphone.cpp
@@ -906,6 +906,5 @@ std::unique_ptr<Module::Configuration> makeConfiguration() {
         deviceConfig.channelMask = AudioChannelLayout{};
         deviceConfig.sampleRate = Int{.value = 0};
-        deviceConfig.gain = AudioGainConfig{};
         deviceConfig.flags = devicePort.flags;
         deviceConfig.ext = devicePort.ext;
         config->initialConfigs.push_back(deviceConfig);
-- 
2.51.0
